<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνώς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶτος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνῶ-ναι</span>): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>unknown</i>, mostly of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνῶτες ἀλλήλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.79
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνὼς πρὸς ἀγνῶτ᾽ εἶπε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					677
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				993
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1008
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πατρί</span>
			<i>clam patre</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				14
			</span></i>: in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῖς ἐν τῇ νηΐ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.137
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				375e
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> of things,
				<i>obscure, unintelligible</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φωνὴ βάρβαρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1051
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1001
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ δόκησις</span>
			<i>dark, vague</i> suspicion, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OT</u>
				681
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>obscure, ignoble</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀκλεής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ. νίκαν</span> a victory
			not <i>unknown to fame</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				2.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.διὰ νεότητα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					3.116b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>ignorant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1133
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τί δύναται</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				20.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> c. gen.,
			where the sense fluctuates between 
				Pass.
			 and 
				Act.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[χθὼν] οὐκ ἀ. θηρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					9.58
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				2.30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγνῶτες ἀλλήλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.53
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀ. τῶν λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>SE</u>
					178a26
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
